- op: discuss  # fa80
  at: '2026-11-17T18:26:29Z'  # fa80
  by: agent  # fa80
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fa80
  clock: 8  # fa80
  nonce: fa80  # fa80
  message: "PR #2234 merged (dev 5e8bcbca0): owed item (1) of my previous note is done. The index keeps the statement records a fold drops, under their version (kept_version / kept_record, last 8 superseded versions per function; 8 is my number), statement_records_at reads a function's records for a given digest and the selector reads through it. Behavioural evidence, live index, 2026-11-17 ~18:20 UTC: after a self-selecting run on the branch folded, statement_records_at(_forget_dead_checkouts at the digest of the branch's first commit, which that fold superseded) returned 22 tests, 22 with a record; before this change that version's records were gone. 15 mutations red. NOT evidence of narrowing at a base: on that branch the base's records were in two first-shape tables I dropped by hand when I changed the table shape, so the base read None. FOUND while checking: smart-test folds only a run that selected for itself or a full run; a run given test files by name is not folded. My runs are mostly by name, so the index's records of many functions were of versions days old (store_edges: the 11-15 version) and the selector answered 'no record of the block as it was'. A full run on dev is in progress to fold every function at dev's version; my pre-PR procedure now starts with one self-selecting run. Item (2), carry-forward, is NOT being built now: it matters only once the selector selects (until then every test that reached a changed function runs and gets a fresh record) and it is sound only for a test the whole change does not affect, i.e. exactly as sound as the selector. It belongs with the switch. Still owed here: (3) the full fold (running), (4) the row names the changed files the selector has no rule for, (5) the new-method rule is a guess. THE ITEM STAYS OPEN."  # fa80
- op: discuss  # 1e56
  at: '2026-11-22T11:15:30Z'  # 1e56
  by: agent  # 1e56
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1e56
  clock: 9  # 1e56
  nonce: '1e56'  # 1e56
  message: "PR #2334: the two owed points that were still open, and the state of the three.\n(3) rows for functions the index had never seen: DONE before this PR. Census at a5b3cca93: 6,806 functions in the six measured packages; 6,758 have a statement record; 25 are in sketch_embeddings.py (omitted from coverage); 23 have a block row and no test pair. (The tracker package is never measured.) New fact: the index spells paths per checkout, so a run from another worktree is UNKNOWN for every block and never narrowed.\n(4) the run row names the changed files the selector has no rule for: files_not_judged landed in PR #2238; its gap is closed here: a change with no package source used to give by_statement null, and now gives the full row with files_not_judged. Rows written before are unchanged.\n(5) the new-method rule is no longer a guess. A new method of an existing class also selects every test that ran the method it overrides (bases read from the class statement, followed through the file's imports to repository source: new module new_def_reach.py). A base that is not repository source answers UNRESOLVED_BASE and nothing is narrowed. A new decorated def and a second def shadowing a name are handled the same safe way. The INV-bifih shape was reproduced as a failing test first: class B(A) gains m; the test paired only with A.m was not selected and narrowing did not refuse; now it is selected. 14 mutations red.\nCLOSE CONDITION, clause by clause: (a) the log exists and a real run has written a row: holds (2,104 rows with answers). (b) each arm has a test with a mutation control: holds; the older arms' mutation tables were not re-run here. (c) an unlisted kind of changed file is reported, not skipped: holds for rows written from this PR on.\nNOT COVERED, filed: a class that gains a method which a subclass lists before another base defining the name; names reached only through getattr; the smart-test bed cannot score this selector (target mode switches it off), so INV-bifih's bed scenario is not added. The item's title still says \"in shadow\": the selector has been live since 2026-11-18, and coverage-select statement-bar today prints MISSED for one run of 2026-11-19 (a failed test left out: test_inv_vopuh_sigpipe.py::test_main_catches_broken_stdout_pipe_and_exits_quietly), which this PR does not address.\n\nFILED FROM THIS: WI-saful (what the new-def rule does not cover; the bed), WI-pikuf (playbook). The probe counted 864 run rows with by_statement null for a YAML or script change, the selector work counted 229 with changed files and no source plus 22 with no change among rows written since the field exists: not reconciled. THE ITEM IS LEFT OPEN (open by owner ruling); its three close-condition clauses hold as stated above."  # 1e56
- op: discuss  # 72cc
  at: '2026-11-22T19:07:02Z'  # 72cc
  by: agent  # 72cc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 72cc
  clock: 10  # 72cc
  nonce: 72cc  # 72cc
  message: "PR #2341 (dev 4e36a3a36): the one thing the item's record still held against the selector is resolved, and the two loose ends are measured.\n\n1. THE MISS. coverage-select statement-bar read MISSED from 2026-11-19 (one run with a failed test left out). The plan's rule for a miss is \"it stays off and is filed\"; neither was done, and my note of 11-22 only mentioned it. Looked at now: the failed test (test_inv_vopuh_sigpipe.py::test_main_catches_broken_stdout_pipe_and_exits_quietly) was edited in the same uncommitted change (snapshot cf2c1c79: its assertion went from rc == 1 to rc == 141 while the `return 1` it checks in cli.main was unchanged). A test written first and run red. The selector was right that no changed statement reached it, and the live narrowing never deselects a test of a changed test file (smart-test hands those files over as `whole`). The count did not know that rule. Fix: evaluate_statement_bar sets aside a failed test whose own file is among the row's changed files, in the miss list and the at-risk list, and prints what it set aside.\n   REPRO RE-RUN on dev 2b1c42d93, 2026-11-22 ~19:10Z: `scripts/coverage-select statement-bar` exits 0 (it exited 1 before): 3,994 rows; a failed test at risk in 191 runs; the selector left tests out in 79 of them (bar 30); RUNS WITH A FAILED TEST LEFT OUT 0; \"failed tests of a changed test file, set aside: 159 in 27 run(s)\"; verdict MET. Before the fix on the same records: 218 / 101 / 1 / MISSED. Output kept: movur_dibin_11222026/dibin/bar_on_dev.txt.\n   One row now reads \"the selector failed\": 2026-11-22T18:23:59Z, written by a mutation control of statement_diff.py (KeyError under the mutation), not by merged code.\n\n2. CLOSE CONDITION, clause (b), re-run today because its tables dated from 11-17: 42 of the older one-line mutations (statement_diff 19, statement_select / coverage-select 8, kept records 15) still apply to the text, 42 red. 9 no longer apply (the code was rewritten); 12 written against today's text, 12 red. With the 11 for this change: 65 mutations, 65 red (one first try did not type-check and was redone). Tables: movur_dibin_11222026/dibin/mutations*.tsv.\n\n3. CARRY-FORWARD (owed point 2 of 11-17, never built): measured instead. A test the narrowing leaves out gets no record of the function's new version, so the next change to that function selects it whole (statement_select: a test with no record of the base version is selected). That costs narrowing, not soundness. On the live index: 492 functions have a kept older version; of their 779,114 test pairs, 34,015 have no record, and 29,888 of those have a record of an older version (the ones a carry-forward would serve). A local `smart-test --full` resets it. Not built; filed.\n\n4. THE TWO COUNTS LEFT UNRECONCILED on 11-22 (864 against 229 + 22): different definitions. 864 = rows with no selector answer whose change names ANY YAML or scripts/ file, over all rows, including the 1,448 written before the field existed (most of them also changed source). Rows written since the field exists (2026-11-17T16:26Z) with changed files and no package source: 246 with no answer today (221 at the time of the probe, 229 a little later), plus 22 with no change at all. Since PR #2334 such a row holds an answer (11 so far).\n\nSTATE. All three clauses of the close condition hold (a: over 2,199 rows hold an answer; b: above; c: files_not_judged, since PR #2334). The selector is live (switched on 2026-11-18 under WI-pugol), so the title's \"in shadow\" describes the item as filed, not the code. NOTHING IS OWED ON THIS ITEM. It is left open only because the lab notebook listed it as \"open by ruling\" and I could not find the ruling's text: closing it is the owner's word.\nNOT COVERED: the count still cannot see the other files a run reads whole (a changed conftest, fixture, or document a gate reads); that errs toward counting a miss that could not happen. Plan step 2c is WI-gapal."  # 72cc
